  "title": "SMB2: fix two memory leaks",
  "description": "* Since c3342930 we don't free anymore the entries in the files hashtables. The cleanest solution is probably to convert these hashtables into two wmem_map_t structures and let the wmem core handling any cleanup.\n    \n* b0f5b2c1749 added supported for chained compression; the uncompressed tvb must be freed\n\n\nTo reproduce the leak, use `pytest`, or, directly, something like:\n\n`tshark -r ./test/captures/smb300-aes-128-ccm.pcap.gz -o 'uat:smb2_seskey_list:1900009c003c0000,\"\",\"\",ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff'`",
